Time Limit: **1 sec**Memory: **256 MB**

##### Description

A cab service company has developed an app that helps drivers manage their daily rides over `N` calendar days. Steven, a driver for this company, wants to maximize his earnings using this app. Each day, Steven can choose to either take a ride within the city, take an inter-city ride, or take no ride at all. However, Steven can only choose an inter-city ride if he took no ride on the previous day. The pay for inter-city rides is always higher than for within-city rides, but inter-city rides have the restriction of needing a day’s gap after any other ride.

You are given two arrays `A` and `B`, where `Ai` and `Bi` represents the cost of the ride within a city and inter-city respectively for the `ith` day. Help Steven to earn the maximum salary in dollars.

##### Input Format

The first line of the input contains an integer `T` - the number of testcases.
`T` testcases follows, where,

The first line of each testcase contains the integer `N`.

The second line of each testcase contains `N` integers representing the array `A`.

The third and last line of each testcase contains `N` integers representing the array `B`.

##### Output Format

For each testcase, output a single line representing the maximum money Steven can make.

##### Constraints

* `1≤T≤103`
* `1≤N≤2×105`
* `1≤Ai<Bi≤103`
* Sum of `N` over all test cases does not exceed `2×105`.

##### Sample Input 1

2 4 10 40 200 20 20 100 210 230 2 1 5 50 50

##### Sample Output 1

330 55

##### Sample Input 2

3 5 20 10 30 50 25 60 40 70 80 90 6 15 20 10 5 25 30 40 35 60 50 70 80 7 5 10 15 20 25 30 35 20 25 30 40 45 50 60

##### Sample Output 2

220 200 160

##### Note

For the first testcase, to earn the maximum salary, Steven must choose inter-city rides on the second day(100) and fourth day(230). So, the maximum salary earned = 100+230=330.

For the second testcase, Steven must choose inter-city ride on first day(50) and within the city ride on 2nd day(5). So, the maximum salary earned = 50+5 = 55.

//rec
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
#define endl "\n"   // optional, better to avoid redefining endl
int rec(int idx, int status, int n, vector<int>& a, vector<int>& b)
{
    if(idx >= n)
        return 0;

    int city = 0;
    int inter = 0;
    int nottake = 0;

    if(status == 0)
    {
        // Previous day = no ride
        city = a[idx] + rec(idx + 1, 1, n, a, b);
        inter = b[idx] + rec(idx + 1, 1, n, a, b);
        nottake = rec(idx + 1, 0, n, a, b);

        return max({city, inter, nottake});
    }
    else
    {
        // Previous day = ride
        // Inter-city NOT allowed
        city = a[idx] + rec(idx + 1, 1, n, a, b);
        nottake = rec(idx + 1, 0, n, a, b);

        return max(city, nottake);
    }
}
void solve() {
    int n;
    cin>>n;
    vector<int>a(n);
    vector<int>b(n);
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        cin>>a[i];
    }

    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        cin>>b[i];
    }

    //starting index, earning,status : 0 (no rest need), 1(prev day need), length
    cout<<rec(0,0,n,a,b)<<endl;
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;
    while (t--) {
        solve();
    }

    return 0;
}



